{
  "id": "airship-editor",
  "title": "Airship / Vessel Editor",
  "stage": 3,
  "status": "editor-alpha",
  "purpose": "Create deep Kaysender airship profiles that connect vessel class, hull culture, core technology, crew, cargo, legal status, route pressure, maintenance burden, faction entanglement, and campaign hooks.",
  "sourceThemes": [
    "Airships are campaign infrastructure: trade machine, mobile base, war platform, escape vehicle, smuggling route, rescue craft, and faction asset.",
    "Airship cores are culturally distinct rather than interchangeable generic engines. Dwarven cores emphasize reliable heavy-duty power, Elven cores are attuned sacred arcane/natural systems, Dragon Kin cores lean into draconic elemental identity, Gnomish cores are hybrid experimental machines, and Human cores blend practical approaches.",
    "Vessel class matters: scouts, patrol craft, frigates, cruisers, liners, destroyers, galleons, and dreadnought-like ships imply different crews, cargos, risks, weapons, and social meaning.",
    "Crew quality and morale can determine whether the mission survives pressure, scarcity, command failure, combat, or route disaster.",
    "Ships should consume and produce other editor outputs: island route pressure, settlement trade access, settlement crisis clocks, faction presence, market cargo, and job-board missions."
  ],
